Renli <oliver.richman@gmail.com> wrote:
> After a few years I decided to pick up playing nethack again.
>
> Played a few times, and believe it or not, after a dozen or so games,
> I got a message "You did not beat your previous score of x points".
> The problem was that on the so-called top 100 list, I was only allowed
> THREE (yes, a whole THREE) entries.

Three entries per Name and Role combination.

That means 39 entries for all roles with the same player names.

> What?! On a single user system - even one shared by a family - that is
> an incredibly annoying thing.

Why "incredibly annoying thing"?

It is, after all, a top score list, although the name "top 100 list"
might be misleading.

If you want have a list of all played games, look for the file called
"logfile".

> I'd go so far as to question if that was really intentional - come on,
> a windows/msdos distrubution with persmax 3?

> Please... Someone should
> really change that. Really.

PERSMAX was already set to 3 in NetHack 1.3d, but I don't know if it
used a different way to trim the score list than the current version.

Being so old, this limitation has probably something to do with space
or cpu time restraints that nowadays are no longer a concern.

> Please... Someone should
> really change that. Really.

You can always write directly to the DevTeam:
http://www.nethack.org/common/contact.html

They might even answer.

And change it.

When the next version comes out. ;-)

